menu "LP jacket stand"

    config LP_STAND_ID
        string "Stand identifier"
        default "lp-stand-01"
        help
            Appears in the MQTT topics and as the client id. Must match the
            stand lightd publishes to: eds/lightstand/<id>/scene.

    config LP_TOPIC_PREFIX
        string "Topic prefix"
        default "eds"
        help
            Root of the topic tree. Must match lightd's LIGHTD_TOPIC_PREFIX.

    menu "Strip"

        config LP_LED_COUNT
            int "Number of LEDs"
            range 1 300
            default 60

        config LP_LED_GPIO
            int "Data GPIO"
            range 0 48
            default 18
            help
                Data line for the WS2812/SK6812 strip. Pick a pin that is not
                strapped at boot, or the strip will flicker during reset.

    endmenu

    menu "Network"

        config LP_WIFI_SSID
            string "WiFi SSID"
            default "DVNTM-IOT"
            help
                The stand belongs on the IoT segment (VLAN 30), where the
                segmentation model puts custom-firmware embedded devices.

                There is no option for the key, on purpose: it is read from
                the creds partition and from nowhere else, so it cannot end
                up in sdkconfig or the image. `make provision` writes it.

        config LP_MQTT_URI
            string "Broker URI"
            default "mqtts://mqtt.mobile.deevnet.net:8883"
            help
                The substrate's broker is TLS only: nothing listens on 1883.
                mqtt:// is for bring-up against a local broker. `mqtt` is a
                service name on IoT Backend (VLAN 35), so the host behind it
                can move without reflashing every stand.

                Normally provisioned rather than set here: `make provision`.

        config LP_MQTT_USERNAME
            string "Broker username"
            default "lp-stand-01"
            help
                The password has no option here, for the same reason the
                WiFi key has none: it is provisioned, never compiled in.

        config LP_MQTT_USE_TLS
            bool "Embed a fallback CA for the broker"
            default n
            help
                Requires main/certs/mqtt_ca.pem. The CA is normally
                provisioned beside the credentials (`make provision`) and this
                is not needed; a provisioned one takes precedence.

    endmenu

endmenu
